"Above all, Africa's future will be decided not merely in diplomatic summits, but in the daily renewal of the social contract between African states and their own citizens—especially young people and women. Strengthening the rule of law, protecting civic freedoms, curbing illicit financial outflows, rooting out corruption, and unleashing the ingenuity of African scientists, artists, farmers, and entrepreneurs are the indispensable foundations upon which external respect rests.",
"Ladies and gentlemen, the twenty-first century will not simply happen to Africa; Africa will help shape the twenty-first century. Let us cast aside inherited fatalism and fragmented rivalry, unite our voices across borders and generations, and build a sovereign, peaceful, innovative, and ecological Africa—not as a pawn in the strategies of others, but as an indispensable pillar of a fairer, more humane world order."
